pipeline: The stages of a pipeline: hosts, steps, and how they roll out.

A pipeline is a file in pipelines/, such as pipelines/site.yaml, or a
key in pipelines of winch.yaml. winch plan site and winch apply site
run it.

Most pipelines run the same steps on every host. Such a pipeline holds
the steps directly, and is one stage with the name of the pipeline. A
pipeline whose hosts have different roles, or that must finish on some
hosts before it starts on others, has stages. They run in order:

```yaml
# pipelines/site.yaml
stages:
  - name: base
    hosts: all
    parallelism: 1
    steps:
      - timezone:
          name: Etc/UTC
  - name: web
    hosts: web
    health:
      command: systemctl is-active nginx
      stable: 10
      timeout: 120
    steps:
      - recipe: nginx
```

```yaml
# winch.yaml
name: acme
inventories:
  production:
    hosts:
      web1.acme.com: {}
      web2.acme.com: {}
    groups:
      web:
        hosts: [web1.acme.com, web2.acme.com]
recipes:
  nginx:
    steps:
      - pkg:
          name: nginx
```

A stage starts when the previous stage finished on all its hosts.
Inside a stage, each host runs its steps in order, without waiting for
other hosts. A stage that matches no host is skipped. --stages runs
only some stages, and --hosts only some hosts.

A step in a stage can use a module directly. It cannot use template,
source, or the key of repo: those read the files of a recipe.

A failed host takes no part in later stages; the other hosts go on. A
new run is the resume: steps that already succeeded check as ok.

Keys:
  stages                 list of maps           -         The stages, in the order they run.
  stages.name            string                 required  The stage name.
  stages.hosts           string                 all       A host pattern.
  stages.parallelism     integer                -         The maximum number of hosts that run the stage at the same time.
  stages.health          map                    -         A health gate: a check that must pass on a host after it finishes the stage, when the stage has a change on that host.
  stages.health.command  string                 required  A command that must exit 0.
  stages.health.stable   integer                0         The seconds that the command must keep exiting 0.
  stages.health.timeout  integer                60        The seconds that the gate has to pass.
  stages.steps           list of steps          required  Recipe steps and module steps, in order.
  stages.handlers        map of lists of steps  -         Named lists of steps of the stage, as in a recipe.
  hosts                  string                 all       The host pattern of the one stage of a pipeline without stages.
  parallelism            integer                -         The maximum number of hosts that run the stage at the same time.
  health                 map                    -         A health gate: a check that must pass on a host after it finishes the stage, when the stage has a change on that host.
  health.command         string                 required  A command that must exit 0.
  health.stable          integer                0         The seconds that the command must keep exiting 0.
  health.timeout         integer                60        The seconds that the gate has to pass.
  steps                  list of steps          -         The steps of the one stage of a pipeline without stages: recipe steps and module steps, in order.
  handlers               map of lists of steps  -         Named lists of steps of the stage, as in a recipe.

Run "winch doc pipeline.<key>" for the full text of a key.
